 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p><b>Bound</b> and <b>constrained</b> properties are bean properties that notify other objects when their value changes.</p><table><tr><th>Point</th><th>Bound Property</th><th>Constrained Property</th></tr><tr><td>Listener interface</td><td>PropertyChangeListener</td><td>VetoableChangeListener</td></tr><tr><td>Event class</td><td>PropertyChangeEvent</td><td>PropertyChangeEvent with veto check</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>After the value changes</td><td>Before the change is finalized</td></tr><tr><td>Rejecting changes</td><td>Cannot stop a change</td><td>Can reject by throwing PropertyVetoException</td></tr><tr><td>Main purpose</td><td>Notify that a value changed</td><td>Validate or restrict a value</td></tr></table><h3>Helper classes</h3><code>PropertyChangeSupport</code> (firePropertyChange) and <code>VetoableChangeSupport</code> (fireVetoableChange).",
 "quiz": {
  "q": "Which property can reject a change?",
  "options": [
   "Bound",
   "Constrained",
   "Indexed"
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "why": "Constrained = Can stop."
 }
